plasma-login-manager (6.7.4-1-soplos) forky; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 6.7.4.
  * Fix the greeter UI language staying in English, or a mix of English and
    the system language, on both fresh Calamares installs and upgrades of
    plasma-login-manager on an already-installed system. plasmalogin writes
    its own plasma-localerc the first time the greeter runs, with a
    hardcoded en_US default, before postinst ever gets a chance to apply
    the real system locale: on a Calamares install the squashfs ships with
    no locale set yet, and on an already-installed system the greeter's
    own first-run default is already on disk by the time this package is
    next upgraded. postinst wrote LANGUAGE only when it found none already
    there, which protected that wrong default forever instead of an actual
    choice. It now overwrites LANGUAGE unconditionally on every install and
    upgrade of this package, deriving it from /etc/default/locale as
    before.

 -- Sergi Perich <info@soploslinux.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200

plasma-login-manager (6.7.2-1-soplos) forky; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 6.7.2, matching the Plasma 6.7.2 shipped by Tyson.
  * Set the greeter UI language from the system locale. The greeter runs as
    the plasmalogin user before any user session exists, so nothing exports
    LANGUAGE for it and it came up in English even though the translations
    were installed. postinst now derives it from LANG and writes it to the
    greeter's plasma-localerc, without overwriting a choice made in the KCM.
  * Raise build dependencies to what 6.7.2 requires: KF6 and ECM 6.26.0,
    Plasma components 6.7.0.
  * Ship a European Portuguese translation in po/pt, adapted from the Brazilian
    one. It is the only Soplos language KDE does not translate.
  * Build with hardening=-fortify. With hardening=+all every CMake feature
    check failed, which is what produced the mistaken belief that development
    packages were installed with their headers missing.
  * Declare the systemd and init-system-helpers dependencies the maintainer
    scripts rely on. Overriding dh_installtmpfiles, dh_installsysusers and
    dh_installsystemd stops debhelper from adding them to misc:Depends, so
    postinst called systemd-tmpfiles, systemd-sysusers and deb-systemd-helper
    with nothing declaring them.
  * Purge now removes /etc/plasmalogin.conf and /var/lib/plasmalogin, which
    postinst and tmpfiles create. The plasmalogin user is left in place.
  * Do not restart plasmalogin.service on upgrade. It killed the running
    graphical session, and doing that during an apt run left the rest of the
    upgrade half configured. The new version now takes effect on the next
    boot, as it does for every display manager in Debian.

 -- Sergi Perich <info@soploslinux.com>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0200

